  "description": "YACLUM crystallizes in the monoclinic crystal system with space group P 21/n. Reported CIF formula moiety: C58 H80 Er4 N8 O20,2(C1 H4 O1),2(H2 O1). From the CIF bond table, Er2 (Er) has 7 O neighbors; Er1 (Er) has 6 O neighbors; Er3 (Er) has 7 O neighbors; Er4 (Er) has 6 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 5 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.649-3.912 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 99.11-113.97°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C58H80Er4N8O20·2(CH4O)·2(H2O). Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 1 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 2 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)).",
